  "question": {
    "text": "Let the position vectors of points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, respectively. Then which of the following statements is true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MhsHS",
      "text": "The points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> are NOT coplanar",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bo0vm",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is the position vector of a point which divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;internally in the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Df2ji",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is the position vector of a point which divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;externally in the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MPciv",
      "text": "The square of magnitude of the vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>95</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
